From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:08:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Redesign the client switcher: DiceBear initials, real
 skill counts, glass panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Rail button icon now shows the active client's own DiceBear "initials"
  avatar (derives letters + a deterministic color straight from the
  client's name) instead of a generic Building2 icon — doubles as a
  quiet "who you're on right now" cue. Same avatar style used for every
  row in the dropdown.
- Dropdown panel now uses surface-glass-3 (the same blurred/translucent
  floating-panel treatment the engagement page's "Modify" menu and the
  home page's workspace-card "..." menu already use via ActionMenu),
  instead of a flat opaque card.
- Each row now shows "N skills enabled" (real data, via a new lazy
  /api/workspaces/summary endpoint + a bulk
  getPrimaryEngagementIdsForWorkspaces helper) instead of a "Team Plan /
  N members" line that never applied to this app's model. Fetched only
  when the switcher is actually opened, not on every page load.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011PX9qLTKPtXba6ncjAwLyN
